Hello Takashi.

On Wednesday 30 July 2008 18:33:36 Takashi Iwai wrote:

> What is this "initial volume problem"?
> Could you compare /proc/asound/card0/codec#* outputs between patched
> and non-patched cases?

I've attached it for both unpatched and patched alsa 1.0.17. I haven't closely 
tested it this time but last time my impression was that the volume was not 
as loud as it should have been. Patching patch_realtek.c fixed it for me.

BTW- for both I've used exactly the same mixer settings.

> > 3) Sound distortions only appear on the center channel while playing back
> >    multi channel content. They sound like voltage sizzling noise. Hard to
> >    explain. Muting all channels but the center channel makes those
> > distortions disappear.
>
> Hm, is it via 5.1 channel output with real 6 channels?

Yes. Simple 2.0 material that's just being duplicated to the other speakers by 
alsa works fine... at least for my ears. :-)

> >    A test under Vista revealed no distortions or anything like it. So a
> > faulty chip is actually pretty unlikely.
>
> A good news, at least :)

More or less. A faulty board would have been really bothersome but at least 
after the swap the problems would have been gone.

> In the recent patch_realtek.c, there are bunch of magical initial
> sequences found, e.g. in alc888_coef_init() or in alc_subsystem_id().
> Can any of them change the output quality?
> alc_fix_pll*() is another magical code, too...

I've seen those... but you are asking the wrong guy here. :-) Open specs would 
be really nice to have.

> HDA codecs are often so delicate.  You must care with love :)

Or replace them with something substantially better and that's what I did. 
Since it seems that this won't be fixed any time soon, I have decided to 
order an Asus Xonar DX and hopefully I won't regret it. For the future, I'll 
keep away from Realtek HD audio chips- at least from those that don't have 
their specs available.

Somewhat off-topic but does SPDIF output properly work on the Xonar DX and do 
the front panel header mic-in and headphone out work _in addition_ to the 
rear panel jacks? Because that's about the only thing I currently worry and 
the card is already ordered. ;-)

Thanks again.

Have a nice day,
matthew.

